        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "nUpAq",
          "name": "why",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "OQHFL",
              "name": "cap",
              "fill": "$accent",
              "content": "WHY COLUMNS, NOT BUBBLES",
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.6
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "tif40",
              "name": "body",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "A bubble puts the speaker on the edge of a message and the recipient nowhere. Every line in a room has both, so both get a column, aligned down the page, and five agents read as a sequence instead of a scatter. The status square stays where the rest of the app puts it: on the agent, in the team, never on a message.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 12,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "eJmV9",
          "name": "why quiet",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "yVUG1",
              "name": "cap",
              "fill": "$accent",
              "content": "WHY NOT WAIT FOR A QUIET TERMINAL",
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 0.6
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "mQ09N",
              "name": "body",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "A quiet terminal is not a finished turn. A model thinking, a slow network call and a long silent command all go quiet mid-turn, and nobody has measured how long each CLI stays silent while it is still working. Delivering on that guess types into a running turn, where a message can be lost with nothing to show for it. So Tars says what it cannot see: the message waits, the team rail counts it, and you send it when the terminal shows the turn is done. The day a CLI starts reporting its turns, NOT SENT becomes QUEUED for it and nothing else in the room changes.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 12,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
