        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "l9xfTb",
          "name": "note",
          "fill": "$text-secondary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Idle is at rest, not stopped: Claude Code reports idle at the end of every turn and keeps its session, so a message to it is written at once. Stopped means Tars holds no live session for the agent: the tick says stopped, computed against the live terminals, or the record has no pty, which stopping, a restart and a provider change all clear. Nothing reaches a stopped agent on its own, and the row under your message says what happened for each one. The start and send flow drawn in Chat · Room · all stopped is not built yet; until it is, this is the copy.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    }
